FujiNet Go Astrocade — milestone log
====================================

Each [x] records what was verified and how, in the family tradition (nothing
is "done" on "it compiles"). The plan is in the approved plan file
make-a-new-version-*.md.

M0 — scaffold  [x]
  [x] root CMakeLists (VERSION single-source, FRONTEND switch, GNUInstallDirs
      at top), .gitignore with !build-aux/, LICENSE
  [x] cmake/Dependencies.cmake — fujinet-firmware pinned to astrocade-bringup
      (20e89ead5); the branch's pico/astrocade is checked at configure time
  [x] cmake/StageFujiProto.cmake — stages the cartridge's own protocol
      sources into core/astro/fuji-generated (identical-by-construction; the
      firmware's emu/apply.sh does the same graft into MAME)
  [x] tools/icons/make-icons.py — dark red #8B0000 (distinct from Apple II's
      bright #F44336); icons rendered and committed under data/icons/
  [x] vendored chips z80.h + z80dasm.h (zlib); disassembler API confirmed
      callback-based and standalone (M0's open risk, resolved)
  verify: cmake -B build -DFRONTEND=none configures; icons render.

M1 — emulator core  [x]
  [x] machine.c (bus, dot-paced loop, IM2 interrupt model), video.c
      (registers, magic funcgen, palette, per-scanline render), sound.c
      (transposed DSP + 48 kHz decimation), host.c (thread, 60.05 Hz pacing,
      frame slot + audio ring), fujinet_cart.c (the one cart device)
  [x] WITH_ASTROCADE_ROMS + tools/roms/embed-roms.py (dev embed, off for
      release) + no_embedded_roms.py compliance ctest
  [x] boot_smoke: BIOS reaches its menu, IM 2 selected, scanline interrupt
      armed, host paces 60.05 fps (the sibling ports' unthrottled-core trap)
  [x] funcgen_test (shift/OR/XOR/flop/expand/intercept vectors), keypad_
      matrix_test (all 24 keys via the real IO decode), mapper_test (astromap
      FLAT/256K/512K/APPBANK + FLAT mirror)
  [x] VALIDATED AGAINST MAME: my framebuffer is pixel-identical to a MAME
      astrocde snapshot for both the SELECT GAME menu and a running game
      (280 ZZZAP "ENTER RACE TIME"). NOTE: Astrocade games run as BIOS-
      interpreted bytecode, so the Z80 PC stays in BIOS ROM even in-game --
      verify launches by the framebuffer, never by cart-space PC.
  verify: cmake --build build && ctest -> 4/4 pass; ROM-less build passes
      no_embedded_roms.py and boot_smoke SKIPs (77) with no BIOS.

M2 — session layer  [x]
  [x] astrosession.[ch] wrapping astro_host, settings.c, paths.c, roms.c
      (BIOS resolve + import by CRC32), session.c, bindings.c (24 keypad +
      2 sysact targets, steal-on-remap + persistence), astro_keymap.c,
      audio_sdl.c (SDL3 pull). astro_session is a separate static lib so
      astro_core stays SDL-free.
  [x] Tests 7/7: no_sdl_link (nm-verified zero SDL in astro_core), session
      (settings persist, option defaults, BIOS import accept/reject, real
      start/stop paints a frame), bindings (defaults/steal/persist/reset).
  NOTE: gamepad_sdl.c deferred -- bindings support gamepad buttons but no SDL
  gamepad polling yet; add with a later milestone (hand controllers).

M3 — GNOME frontend + keypad + ROM import  [x]
  [x] GTK4/libadwaita: display (4:3 letterbox, frame-clock pull), header-bar
      menu, keyboard capture via the bound table, Preferences (BIOS variant +
      RAM expansion), system-ROM import by CRC + "no ROM" prompt, FujiNet
      Configuration -> system browser (gtk_uri_launcher).
  [x] keypad window: 6x4 grid faithful to the hardware (gold right column),
      press/release GtkGestureClick, System row (Reset Game / Reset to
      CONFIG), Map row (remap via bindings). F9 toggles; singleton hide-on-close.
  [x] app-id online.fujinet.go.astrocade.gnome; .desktop + metainfo validated
      (desktop-file-validate, appstreamcli --pedantic ctests).
  verify: ran on live Wayland (grim) -- BIOS boots to SELECT GAME with FUJINET
      CONFIG as entry 1; keypad window matches the reference photo. Full ctest 9/9.
M4 — FujiNet end-to-end (runtime build, ports 11500/11501, boot swap)  [x]
  [x] tools/fujinet/build-fujinet-desktop.sh + support/fujinet_desktop_entry.cpp
      + patches/ transposed from the Intv port (target-agnostic); PC_TARGET=
      RS232, force_boip_config port 11500. Builds libfujinet.so (6 MB) from the
      astrocade-bringup branch -- verified (firmware's own tests pass).
  [x] cmake/FujiNetRuntime.cmake (real): WITH_FUJINET builds + installs the
      runtime; the add_custom_command drives the script. dev/install path
      resolution via ASTRO_DEV_FUJINET_OUT / ASTRO_INSTALL_{LIB,DATA}DIR.
  [x] core/src/fujinet_runtime.c: dlopen libfujinet (never dlclose), start/
      stop, wait_for_boip, copy_log; FUJINET_WEBUI_BIND=11501, FUJINET_RUNTIME_
      ROOT set. paths_provision_fujinet copies fnconfig.ini+data+SD into
      <data>/fujinet on first run. session_start brings FujiNet up first then
      waits <=3s for the BoIP listener before the emulator dials in.
  [x] fixed resolve_lib_dir loop terminating on a NULL getenv (skip, not stop).
  verify: the GNOME app itself LISTENS on 127.0.0.1:11500 (BoIP) and :11501
      (web UI, HTTP 200); the log shows "BoIPChannel connected" + "fujinet:
      connected to 127.0.0.1:11500" -- the emulator's cart dials into its own
      in-process FujiNet. session_test exercises the real startup. ctest 10/10.
  TODO: boot-swap/stream end-to-end needs a TNFS host to fully exercise; the
      protocol path is already corpus-verified upstream. FujiNet Console Log
      viewer menu item (function exists) -- minor follow-up.

M5 — debugger (Z80 tab + video-chip tab; all registers)  [x]
  [x] engine (core/debugger/debugger.c): instruction-hook based, pause blocks
      the emu thread in the hook (cond_wait); step/step-over (CALL/RST/DJNZ/
      block-repeat)/step-out (word at SP + SP guard); regs (full Z80 incl.
      shadow bank, IX/IY, I/R, IM, IFF1/2, WZ, HALT); non-destructive peek +
      real poke; 64 breakpoints; stop_serial polled by UI. chips z80dasm.
  [x] video view (core/debugger/vidview.c + astrovid.h): one consistent
      snapshot exposing EVERY register (Nutting pp.106-107) -- 8 color regs,
      mode, HORCB split+bg, VERBL, INFBK/INMOD/INLIN, XPAND, intercept +
      feedback, full magic-funcgen internals, the 8 sound regs + osc/vibrato/
      noise state; renders screen (shares the MAME-validated line code),
      screen-RAM bitmap, 512-pen palette strip, decoded register text.
  [x] GNOME debugger window (F12 / View menu): Z80 tab (controls, registers,
      disassembly with breakpoint markers, hex memory view, addr/bp entries)
      + Video chip tab (screen, screen RAM, palette, all-registers text).
      Shared RGBA scratch sized to MAX of all renders.
  verify: debug_test passes (pause, IM 2 regs, step advances, disassembly,
      repeatable peek, a breakpoint fires exactly at its address, snapshot
      exposes INLIN/VERBL + magic register text). Video renders dumped
      headlessly: register decode correct, 512-pen palette + screen render
      confirmed. Full ctest 10/10.

